Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:22:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wshom: Environment types, SpecialFolders, Shortcut,
 RegDelete, Exec exit code and pipes, Network (3010)

WScript.Shell:
- Environment(type) honours System, User, Volatile and Process: values live in
  the matching registry key (a change is broadcast with WM_SETTINGCHANGE) or in
  the process environment; Item, Count, Length, Remove and enumeration work.
- SpecialFolders resolves all sixteen documented names, has Count and
  enumeration, and returns Empty for an unknown name.
- RegDelete deletes a value, or a key with everything below it.
- Exec: ExitCode; the child now inherits the redirected standard handles, so
  StdIn, StdOut and StdErr actually carry data.
- Shortcut: FullName, Description, Hotkey, RelativePath, TargetPath getters and
  Load; CreateShortcut on an existing file loads it.
- AppActivate (by title or process id), SendKeys (+ ^ % ~ groups, {KEY n}),
  LogEvent (event log).

WScript.Network: UserProfile, Organization, Site, MapNetworkDrive,
RemoveNetworkDrive, EnumNetworkDrives, Add/RemovePrinterConnection,
EnumPrinterConnections, SetDefaultPrinter, AddWindowsPrinterConnection.

